        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2024-03-25T17:58:06.299Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "637219ac5575480f66f16df5",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Face tracking is starting to become standard, and consumes a huge chunk of params. Avatar state is another one which people are consuming it for synced purposes.\n\nIdeally there would be native face tracking and state systems which would preclude the need to run OSC or stash things in params to get around this; but realistically it's not going to happen. \n\nSo in liu of you implementing native solutions which wouldn't consume parameter space, please:\n\n**  Update the param space to a word instead of a byte. **\n\n Double bonus points if you put in a short-short 4-bit integer option.\n\nThis would push from 256 bits to 65.5k which would at least give a lot more headroom.\n\nThe issue here is, the community has already worked around this with animation layers and local parameter stuff. So now you have drastically more complex animation layers just to get around you limiting the parameter size. You've traded one byte of network for basically every avatar running multiple frame sweeps to pack and unpack synced params.\n\nThe community will get around this, you're just making it less efficent. Please just do the right thing and either provide native resources to remove the things consuming large amount of parameter space _OR_ update param space to something that isn't a constant burden and (ideally) increase OSC response time.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
